= Material Assign =

#type: node
#context: sop
#internal: a3ob_material_assign
#tags: arma, p3d

"""Sets the texture and the material (rvmat) of the polygons in a group, or of all polygons."""

A polygon in a P3D file has a texture and a material (an rvmat file). This node sets them for the polygons in a group, or for all polygons.

@inputs

LOD geometry:
    Input 1.

@parameters

Group:
    #id: group

    Which polygons to set. Empty means all polygons. Normal Houdini group syntax; a selection with an encoded name is easiest to pick in the Selection browser.

    Type: Text. Default: (empty).

Group Type:
    #id: grouptype

    Type: Menu. Default: Primitives.

    Primitives:
        the polygons in the group.

    Points:
        the polygons whose points are all in the group.

Set Texture:
    #id: settex

    Off: leave a3ob_texture as it is.

    Type: On or off. Default: On.

Texture Source:
    #id: texsource

    Where the texture text comes from.

    Type: Menu. Default: File.

    File:
        Sets this to File.

    Color:
        Sets this to Color.

    Custom:
        Sets this to Custom.

Texture File:
    #id: texture

    For File. Slashes are written as backslashes.

    Type: Text. Default: (empty).

Color:
    #id: color

    For Color. Red, green, blue and alpha, 0 to 1.

    Type: 4 numbers. Default: 1, 1, 1, 1.

Color Type:
    #id: colortype

    For Color. The kind of procedural texture.

    Type: Menu. Default: CO - Color Value.

    CO - Color Value:
        Sets this to CO - Color Value.

    CA - Texture with Alpha:
        Sets this to CA - Texture with Alpha.

    LCO - Terrain Texture Layer Color:
        Sets this to LCO - Terrain Texture Layer Color.

    SKY - Sky texture:
        Sets this to SKY - Sky texture.

    NO - Normal Map:
        Sets this to NO - Normal Map.

    NS - Normal map specular with Alpha:
        Sets this to NS - Normal map specular with Alpha.

    NOF - Normal map faded:
        Sets this to NOF - Normal map faded.

    NON - Normal map noise:
        Sets this to NON - Normal map noise.

    NOHQ - Normal map High Quality:
        Sets this to NOHQ - Normal map High Quality.

    NOPX - Normal Map with paralax:
        Sets this to NOPX - Normal Map with paralax.

    NOVHQ - two-part DXT5 compression:
        Sets this to NOVHQ - two-part DXT5 compression.

    DT - Detail Texture:
        Sets this to DT - Detail Texture.

    CDT - Colored detail texture:
        Sets this to CDT - Colored detail texture.

    MCO - Multiply color:
        Sets this to MCO - Multiply color.

    DTSMDI - Detail SMDI map:
        Sets this to DTSMDI - Detail SMDI map.

    MC - Macro Texture:
        Sets this to MC - Macro Texture.

    AS - Ambient Shadow texture:
        Sets this to AS - Ambient Shadow texture.

    ADS - Ambient Shadow in Blue:
        Sets this to ADS - Ambient Shadow in Blue.

    PR - Ambient shadow from directions:
        Sets this to PR - Ambient shadow from directions.

    SM - Specular Map:
        Sets this to SM - Specular Map.

    SMDI - Specular Map, optimized:
        Sets this to SMDI - Specular Map, optimized.

    MASK - Mask for multimaterial:
        Sets this to MASK - Mask for multimaterial.

    TI - Thermal imaging map:
        Sets this to TI - Thermal imaging map.

Raw Text:
    #id: raw

    For Custom. Copied exactly as typed.

    Type: Text. Default: (empty).

Common Procedural:
    #id: commonproc

    Fill Raw Text from the common procedural textures (and switch Texture Source to Custom). Add your own in the common data file of the Project root and presets tool.

    Type: Menu. Default: none.

    The choices are made when you open the menu, from the geometry or the settings.

Set Material:
    #id: setmat

    Off: leave a3ob_material as it is.

    Type: On or off. Default: On.

Material File:
    #id: material

    The rvmat path. Empty clears the material. Slashes are written as backslashes.

    Type: Text. Default: (empty).

Add Common:
    #id: commonmat

    Fill Material File from the common materials (and switch Set Material on). Add your own in the common data file of the Project root and presets tool.

    Type: Menu. Default: none.

    The choices are made when you open the menu, from the geometry or the settings.

The full page for this node is docs/user/reference/a3ob_material_assign.html in the A3OB folder. Open it in a web browser.
